  "id": "successive-contrast",
  "term": "successive contrast",
  "definition": "Successive contrast is the apparent change in the colour or brightness of a surface caused by earlier stimulation of the same area of the retina by a different light. In plain terms, it is the effect of an after-image falling on a newly viewed surface.",
